## STANDING LINES
1. **PRIOR-WORK CHECK, before the first git write in your clone.** Read whole: RD-885, RD-849 and RD-876 by Jira GET (`/rest/api/3/issue/<key>?fields=summary,status,description,comment`; any JQL begins `project = RD AND (...)` WITH the parentheses; use the read helper rule: load `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/HPSM-POC/.tools/b653/jira.py` with `python3 -I` through `importlib` and call `api("GET", ...)`, `api("POST", "/rest/api/3/search/jql", ...)` for search only, or `show`, after reading it whole; it reads the HPSM-POC project's `.env` in-process and never prints it); RD-801 and RD-802 (summary and status), RD-777/-776/-882 (summary and status); the B714 gate's STATUS `Briefs/2026-10-26_B714_STATUS.md` lines 150-165 and its evidence folder `Briefs/2026-10-26_B714_evidence/` (for the C4 and C5 probes: read-allowed, a finished seat's); the B703 STATUS (`Briefs/2026-10-25_B703_STATUS.md`) for how the counts were regenerated and landed; `CLARIFICATIONS.md` by line range (the Read tool refuses it whole): C-133 (`:1434`) and its addenda (`:1448`), C-190 (`:2062`) with `:2067`, `:2068`, `:2073`, `:2076`, C-68 (`:665`), C-202 (`:2187`), C-209 (`:2270`), C-218 (`:2362`); `/usr/bin/grep -n -E 'RD-(885|849|876|801|802)|logSafe' CLARIFICATIONS.md | cut -c1-300` (control: the pattern `RD-zzz9` prints none); in your clone `git --no-optional-locks log --format='%h %s' -8 -- backend/logSafe.js`, and the same for `backend/simpleDb.js`, `__tests__/helpers/dockerfile-stages.js`; open PRs and `refs/heads/b6*`, `b7*`, `records/*` (if any touches your paths, that ticket is STARTABLE NO). **A READY FOR QA, a PARTIAL or a STOPPED without a PRIOR WORK section naming what you read and found is returned unread.** The PRIOR WORK section must say what each change PRESERVES, each with the cell or measurement that holds it: RD-885: the 183-green R8 behaviour on the unmutated product, every other rd777/rd618/rd848 cell title unchanged (except the 4 accounted renames), `dockerfile-stages.js` readers green; RD-849: the CR/LF removal and its position, the C0 and separator escapes, TAB kept, the ordinary-string cell, the 500-character cap, `rd802` green; RD-876: the caller limit below 1000 honoured, the floor of 1, the default 100, `T0` (50 rows), `T11` (22 rows) and every cell that passes 10000, and nothing about who may call the endpoint.
2. **No production, no demo, no hosted site, no HTTP to any hosted host, no `az`, no Kudu, no docker, no ssh other than git's own `core.sshCommand`.** The only outbound traffic is what `npm ci` / `npm rebuild`, `git fetch`/`git push`, GitHub GETs and the Jira GETs themselves do, plus the loopback servers jest cells bind on `127.0.0.1`. Never set, read-to-change or touch the repo variable `CI_DEPLOY_ENABLED`, a secret, an environment, or the repo's Actions settings. GitHub's core limit is shared (5000 an hour) and `search/code` is throttled (30 a minute): poll no faster than the heartbeat says and never in a tight loop.
3. **No message to any human.** No mail, chat or PR comment. No person's name and no decision-card id in STATUS, code comments, commit messages or branch names (say "the product owner"; git author fields carry a name: do not quote them). Nothing to the client. Client name: Datasec/NexusAI only. **Jira is READ ONLY for you (GET only; zero writes);** ticket transitions and the project's records are the records seat's, after the landing.
4. **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -d/-D`, `--prune`, `update-ref -d`, `worktree remove`, `worktree prune`, `gc`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `checkout -- <file>`). Quarantine to `session-tools/b746/_quarantine/`. Restoring a mutated file is done by writing `git show HEAD:<path>` over it and proving equality by hash and `git diff --quiet`, never by `checkout --`. Never rebase, amend, squash or force-push. Never write in the shared checkout `2_Project_Files` (read `git status --porcelain | wc -l` before and after, equal). Never open, read or write another seat's tree or kit: `worktrees/b[0-9][0-9][0-9]-*` other than your own `worktrees/b746-fix`, `session-tools/b[0-9][0-9][0-9]*` other than your own `session-tools/b746/`, and any `worktrees/**` you did not create (a finished seat's STATUS file and the Briefs evidence folders are read-allowed). **Commit corrections as a NEW commit only while the branch is local; once pushed, a correction is a STOP for Tuesday, not an amend.**
5. **Shell:** never type `cd` (a hook refuses it); absolute single-quoted paths (they contain `!`); `git -C`; read git with `--no-optional-locks`; `bash -c '...'` or a heredoc for chains and loops (zsh does not split an unquoted `$VAR`; a hook refuses it); `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; write `${VAR}:path`, never `$VAR:path`; no unquoted word starting with `=` (use `echo ----`); write STATUS and source files with the editor tool; never hand-edit `package-lock.json`. Never kill a process by basename: by pid/port plus cwd. Stop every process you start and record the ports free again.
6. **Record every choice a reader would ask about** in STATUS under DESIGN with its source. At least: **D1** the order of the three tickets and why one branch (the shared counts file); **D2** the counts arithmetic per commit (cells added per ticket by `jest --json`, the file's value before and after, each equal to the verify); **D3** for RD-885, where the git-environment fix sits and why (the helper versus the cells), and the C4/C5 probes; **D4** for RD-849, the escape form chosen for C1 and why it matches the C0 form, and that the CR/LF barrier is untouched; **D5** for RD-876, the constant's name and place, the seed size found, the cells that pass 10000 and that none moved; **D6** what each mutant proved; **D7** what you did NOT widen (RD-878, RD-870, the `simpleDb.js:305` limit, the notice and the button, who may call the endpoint); **D8** why the whole verify is run at the final head (the pinned counts are the CI predicate; arithmetic is the plan, the run is the proof).
